<article class="history-essay"><nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">English edition</a> / <a href="/en/magazine/">Cultural magazine</a></nav><header><p class="eyebrow">HISTORY OF NINETEENTH-CENTURY ARGENTINA · DOCUMENTED ESSAY</p><h1>Indigenous Peoples and Argentina’s Southern Frontier</h1><p class="deck">The frontier was not a fixed line between a settled country and an empty wilderness. It was a shifting region of Indigenous territories, state expansion, negotiation, commerce and violence.</p></header><figure><img src="/media/revista/frontera-pueblos-indigenas.webp" alt="Modern editorial reconstruction illustrating the nineteenth-century Argentine frontier" loading="eager"/><figcaption>Modern editorial illustration. Not an archival photograph.</figcaption></figure><div class="article-body"><nav class="toc" aria-label="Article contents"><strong>In this article</strong>{sections.map(s=><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.heading}</a>)}<a href="#source-notes">Sources and reading</a></nav>{sections.map((s,i)=><><section id={s.id}><h2>{s.heading}</h2><p>{s.body}</p></section>{i===0&&<AdSlot id="article-02-after-intro" kind="article"/>}{i===2&&<AdSlot id="article-03-middle" kind="article"/>}{i===3&&<AdSlot id="article-04-late" kind="article"/>}</>)}<section id="source-notes"><h2>Sources and editorial method</h2><p>This original English article follows documented themes in the Spanish research edition, while maintaining a distinction between historical evidence, modern interpretation and the fictional testimony of Martín Fierro. Linked sources remain under their custodians’ control.</p><ul>{sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.name}</a></li>)}</ul><h3>Read the poem in its original Spanish</h3><p>{cantos.map(c=><a class="canto" href={`/leer/ida/${c}/`} lang="es">El gaucho Martín Fierro — Canto {c} ↗</a>)}</p><p><a href="/en/magazine/">← More English cultural essays</a> · <a href="/en/what-is-martin-fierro/">Introduction to Martín Fierro</a></p></section></div><AdSlot id="article-05-after-article" kind="article"/>
</article>
